  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on the node's rule and witnesses: 10 witnesses, all with the expected verdicts.\n\nI broke the one-command rule twice, so up to four of the six gate runs may have been charged:\n- **First mistake:** I ran the gate with its output thrown away, before editing anything, so I never saw that verdict.\n- **Second mistake:** I ran it on the untouched skeleton when I meant to read a file. It returned `UNUSED_CLAIM`, as expected for the empty placeholders.\n- **Third run (real):** returned `VACUOUS`. The rule's check that a right turn lane enters the intersection being judged changed no witness's result. I added a witness (`branch_6`) where an aligned right turn lane enters a different intersection, which the rule should report as violated.\n- **Fourth run:** returned `OK`.\n\nHow the rule reads the node:\n- **\"At the observation before entry\":** the formula language has no \"previous observation\" operator. I wrote that moment as `rises(occupies(subject, i) ∨ ¬X)`; combined with the entry into intersection `i`, this means exactly \"X held at the observation before.\" The declared right-turn intention is read there, never after the judged moment.\n- **\"Has a right turn lane\":** this means exactly one turn lane on the right side that enters the intersection and runs the same way as the subject's lane or roadway. \"Same way\" means the cosine between their directions is at or above `p.approach_lane_same_direction_cos`. The rule applies only when there is no such single lane.\n- **Obligation:** at that same observation, the subject must be in a lane entering the intersection whose ordinal equals the lane count, i.e. the rightmost lane. If it is in no such lane, it must be on an unlaned roadway segment that enters the intersection. The obligation repeats the full selection of the intersection and applies at every intersection selected.\n- **Narrowings:** I declared none, because the encoding says exactly what the record says.\n\nI added five witnesses beyond the planned six:\n\n| witness | expected | what it shows |\n|---|---|---|\n| `branch_3` | violated | two right turn lanes, so there is no single one |\n| `branch_4` | violated | the only right turn lane serves the opposite approach |\n| `branch_5` | violated | the turn lane on the approach is a left turn lane |\n| `branch_6` | violated | an aligned right turn lane enters a different intersection |\n\nI found nothing wrong with the node itself. Each gate run, the encoding and every witness are recorded in `task_result.md` in the working directory.",
